    "interpreted": "Loaded and executed by the donor's IOP interpreter, as every game IRX is today (docs/IOP-MAP.md). No host model needed.",
    "interpreted_no_device": "Loaded and interpreted, but the module drives DEV9/SMAP/PPP hardware that this runtime does not model. Expected behaviour: the module loads, its device open fails or returns 'no device'. A hang here is a S7b finding; the fallback order is a per-module instruction counter, then an HLE stub that reports 'no network device', then refusal to load.",
